{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>Who dwelt in Egypt thirty years and four hundred years.</b> The completion of four hundred and thirty years from the day He brought Abraham our father out of Ur of the Chaldees to bring him into the covenant between the pieces, as it says there (Genesis 15:7): אֲנִי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאוּר כַּשְׂדִּים — and therefore they said in Seder Olam: Abraham our father was seventy years old at the covenant between the pieces."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:17.785200555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}